  "description": "QUZBIZ crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C102 H87 Dy5 N7 O26 P1,4(C1 H4 O1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy5 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 6 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.559-3.838 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 96.08-112.82°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Dy5(L)6(Ph3PO)(NO3)(H2O)2(μ3-OH)2]. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 1 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 1 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 2 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 2 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)). Article name explicitly identifies Dy(III).",
